From 7b6cef462892942c3597329eefb4189265f7d09f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 17:51:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 862/913] product/tfm-stm32mp2: update trace in tfm modules

Cleanup the traces in stm32mp2 tfm modules:
- align coding style and trace style for each module
- remove usage of PRIx32/PRIx8, not supported in TF-M
- in module tfm regulator consumer:
  - add prefix MOD_NAME
  - change FWK_LOG_INFO to FWK_LOG_DEBUG
  - remove PMIC reference: other SCMI regulators are exported by TF-M
    (for example PWR)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git f3967b69df012b47c6b5ec66c708f420221f73d1 product/tfm-stm32mp2: update trace in tfm modules]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I3abf5a06db6330b80d07a513a9b6023cf301d23d
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/SCP-firmware/+/587593
Tested-by: Valentin CARON <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Valentin CARON <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Valentin CARON <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
